# Cookies — notify before implementation

Before **implementing or merging** any feature that uses **cookies** (or equivalent client identifiers stored like cookies), **stop and notify the project owner for explicit approval first**. Do not land cookie code “quietly.”

## What counts

- `document.cookie`, `Set-Cookie` / server-set cookies, or libraries that set first-party cookies  
- Third-party scripts whose primary role is tracking/consent cookies (e.g. analytics that rely on cookies)  
- Any change that **updates the privacy policy** or user-facing claims about data collection because of cookies  

## What to include in the notification

A short plan: **purpose**, **what is stored**, **who can read it** (first vs third party), **lifetime**, and whether **`privacy.html`** (or related copy) must change.

## After approval

Implement only what was approved; if scope grows, pause and confirm again.
